export anchor BoardingPassStyle:
    number: 69
    screen: TodayMobile
    name: Boarding pass
    idea: Every meeting is a line on a departure board and every task a paper ticket with a torn-off stub, so the day reads like a travel itinerary.
    base: light
    palette:
        tarmac: #e7e9ec, the page behind the tickets and the round notch cut-outs
        ticket: #fffdf8, ticket bodies, the header pass and the nav strip
        stub: #f3efe4, the tear-off stub on the right of each ticket
        navyInk: #15233f, text, the header band, gate signs and the Due today stamp
        slate: #4d5a70, field captions and the Upcoming stamp
        perforation: #9aa3b2, dashed tear lines, decorative only
        signalOrange: #b23c0c, the add button, the priority tag, the badge and focus
        board: #1b2433, the departure board panel for meetings
        flap: #f6f3e8, split-flap digit tiles on the board
        clearedGreen: #1d6b45, the Done stamp with a tick
        delayRed: #a8201a, the Overdue stamp with a triangle and the overdue ticket ring
    type:
        Two families. Condensed sans is Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed,
        Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif, used for names, headings and
        caps captions. Monospace is ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo,
        Consolas, monospace, used for codes, counts, times and field values.
        Body falls back to system-ui. Sizes are 26px bold mono for the
        manifest counts, 20px bold mono gate codes, 18px bold condensed caps
        for header values, 17px bold condensed task names, 15px bold mono on
        flap tiles, 13px bold mono field values and 10px bold condensed caps
        captions with 0.14em tracking.
    layout:
        A single phone column up to 400px wide centred on the tarmac grey
        with generous space around it. The header is a boarding pass with a
        navy band holding a paper plane mark, the brand in spaced caps and
        the avatar, then Passenger and Date fields and a route line reading
        6 TSK to 2 MTG with a small plane, plus the line 6 tasks, 2
        meetings. Each section opens with a navy gate sign, a dashed rule
        and a two digit count. Meetings sit in a dark departure board table
        with split-flap time digits, the name in caps and a Next or Later
        remark. Each task is a ticket with a flight number such as BW 101,
        the name, and Project and Due fields, joined by a dashed perforation
        with round notches to a 92px stub showing the gate code and a status
        stamp. The bottom bar is a ticket strip with a dashed top edge, four
        tabs and a raised round orange add button in the middle.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between tickets, 12 to 14px ticket padding, 28px before each gate sign.
    density: Medium. About five tickets fit on one phone screen.
    corners: 10 to 14px on tickets, the header and the board, 2 to 3px on stamps and gate signs, round avatar and add button.
    borders: 2px dashed perforations between ticket and stub. Stamps use 1.5 to 2px outlines. The overdue ticket gets a 2px red ring.
    shadows: A 1px hard bottom edge in #c9ced6 plus 0 4px 10px navy at 8 percent, like paper on a desk.
    icons:
        2px stroke line icons with square ends at 22px in the nav. A paper
        plane is the brand mark. Status stamps pair a word with a filled
        dot for Due today, a hollow ring for Upcoming, a tick for Done and a
        triangle for Overdue. The done stamp is tilted six degrees and the
        done name is struck through.
    focus: A 3px signal orange outline offset 2px on buttons, fields and rows.
    tone: Travel words as short caps labels, such as Passenger, Gate, Departures and Boarding. Task names stay plain sentence case.
